<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Vendor-private Vulkan extensions of the proton-mac (PMW) fork. Not part of the
Khronos registry. Merged into Mesa's generators (vk_extensions, dispatch table,
entrypoints, command queue) next to vk.xml; the C declarations are in
include/vulkan/vk_pmw_metalfx.h and must match this file. The same fragment is
meant to be merged into winevulkan's vk.xml so make_vulkan can thunk it: only
plain handles, POD structs and scalars cross the API, no Metal objects.

Extension number 90001 is far outside the Khronos range, so its enum offsets
(1000000000 + 90000 * 1000 + offset) cannot collide with a real extension.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
-->
